# Vault conventions

- Preserve the PARA roots: `00_Inbox`, `20_Projects`, `30_Areas`, `40_Resources`, and `50_Archives`.
- Keep journals in `10_Journals` and operational views in `90_Dashboards`.
- Store reusable templates in `99_Templates`.
- Default uncategorized notes to `00_Inbox`; do not guess a permanent location without evidence.
- Keep folders shallow. Express meaning through links, properties, tags, and MOCs.
- Exception: places may nest under `40_Resources/Places` as `country → region → city → attraction` with Folder Notes (`Name/Name.md`). Trips also use Folder Notes at `20_Projects/Trips/<Trip>/<Trip>.md` with sibling `days/`, `tips/`, `prep/`, and `assets/` folders.
- Do not use Pretty Properties `icon` frontmatter; banners may still use `banner` / `banner_position`.
- Use ISO dates (`YYYY-MM-DD`) in properties.
- Preserve established property names: `type`, `status`, `created_date`, `area`, `project`, `due`, `review_date`, and `target_date`.
- Place notes also use `place_type`, `parent` (wiki link; empty only for countries), `map_url` (Google Maps link for phone use), and `location` (`[lat, lng]` for Map View).
- Recipe notes live in `40_Resources/Recipes` with `type: recipe`, plus `cuisine`, `meal`, `servings`, and optional timing fields.
- Use wiki links for vault entities and hierarchical tags only for broad cross-cutting topics.
- Never edit generated community-plugin bundles (`main.js`, `styles.css`) by hand.
